       exists only in the builder's report. But the Acceptance bullet says the outputs
       are "in the build log", and "the build log" names no artefact this officina
       defines or produces — the phrase appears nowhere in docs/ADOPTION.md,
       docs/STUDIO.md or any lex, and only in W-046's own brief. studio/ci/ holds gate
       certificates and reds, nothing else, and CLAUDE.md lists ci/*.log under "Never
       by hand". The builder therefore had no compliant committed location available
       and could not have manufactured one without breaking a standing rule.
       The bullet's substantive half — that the eight shipped names are the ones
       step 0 showed flipping — is what actually protects the policy, and I ran it
       myself: §2 above records all three outputs verbatim and discharges it.
       For the fix list: the wording should name a real artefact, because as written
       it made an acceptance gate verifiable by nobody except the builder.

  O-2  The builder's aborted mid-build `verify` — RULING: honest in substance,
       undisclosed durably. Not a blocking finding; a recurrent class.
       Self-reported: the builder ran the forbidden `verify` mid-build, reverted with
