## 8. Verdict

  FAIL, round 1.

  Two blocking findings, both about what the opus CLAIMS rather than what it built:
  F-1, a live network egress channel that the signed limit denies having, measured
  under the shipped argv with a hallucination control; and F-2, a fail-closed path
  that is silent where an explicit Acceptance condition and the shipped documentation
  both say it names the model.

  Everything else stands up, and the round should be read that way. All gates green
  and re-run by me. Thirty of thirty mutations caught. The codex half of the live
  smoke passes outright, including the resume case Sol raised and stubs could not
  reach, and the write refusal binds live through talk on a resumed session. Step 0
  re-run from scratch confirms every CLI fact the policy rests on. The code is
  faithful to the brief; the brief is wrong in two places and the builder carried
  both faithfully into shipped artefacts. The fixes are documentary plus one shared
  guard and one behaviour — small, and they belong in one round.

  Both blocking findings touch docs/ADOPTION.md, the codex.ts header and behaviour 6
  together. Dispatch them as one change, not three: F-1 and F-2 are one class of
  defect — a claim asserted in a tested document that the live vendor refutes.
